  [RISK] arch/riscv/Kconfig:279-285  
      CONFIG_RISCV_M_MODE depends on !MMU, meaning the PMP code in head.S is only compiled for nommu M-mode kernels — not for standard S-mode Linux. There is no CONFIG_RISCV_SMEPMP, CONFIG_RISCV_PMP, or CONFIG_RISCV_M_SECCFG anywhere in Kconfig. The kernel has zero build-time awareness of Smepmp as a feature. Implicit invariant: for S-mode kernels, PMP/mseccfg configuration is exclusively the responsibility of M-mode firmware (e.g., OpenSBI), and the kernel blindly trusts that firmware has configured Smepmp correctly. There is no Kconfig assertion that the platform supports Smepmp, no way to assert 'this kernel requires Smepmp enforcement', and no way to detect at build time whether the bootloader will provide it.
  [RISK] arch/riscv/include/asm/sbi.h:426-446  
